								<p class="newsTitle">
									Winds of Change - 
									10/18/2005 10:52:56 PM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									Today we're sad to see our dear Tank Lead, Rhazzor, move on in EQ life.&nbsp; After seven happy months with DoR he's been called to service in his guild.&nbsp; We know they'll be just as proud of him as we are!<br /> <br /> It was a good last day, though, as tonight saw our final defeat of Agnarr, the Storm Lord, and I think our smoothest raid against him yet.&nbsp; Now we're left to our devices with RZTW, Sol Ro, and his minis (and, by a slight oversight, one more raid against VZ).&nbsp; Stay tuned for more conquests and our first expeditions into the Elemental Planes!<br /> 
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									The Elements are in the Air - 
									9/26/2005 4:12:57 PM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									Hello DORians.......<br /><br />We have sucessfully knocked off Lord Mithaniel Marr!! Congrats to all that recieved his flag and a BIG thank you to all of you that stuck in there to help your fellow raiders.&nbsp; As you know we are getting close to the Elementals ~ Plane of Earth, Plane of Water, Plane of Air, &amp; Plane of Fire ~ For all of those new to the game or returning Planes of Power Gods can be a push over compared to the new Gods in GoD, OoW, DoN, and DoD.&nbsp; However, the Elemental Gods are a Challenge! Concentration and your undivided attentation to quick changes in strategies will make the Elementals run smoothly.<br /><br /><br />
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									Take a deep breath - 
									8/25/2005 5:34:21 AM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									Well we did it, Saryrn has been bested 4 times each time a WIN congrats goes out to all you OR raiders and leaders!&nbsp; On Friday Aug. 19 OR had their first win aganist Agnarr....woot way to go Jetta for leading it and to all the raiders that attended, for those that went above and beyond "hats off to you all". <br />Now we have added Rallos Zek the Warlord.......muhahaha Please give us time to get our game plans together before our first encounter. If you have never encountered him, he is the very tough to beat and will need your FULL UNDIVIDED ATTENTION from start to finish. Many guilds fail him many times over before a win so be prepared.<br />Current targets on rotation now are: TZ/VZ (last one coming soon), LMM, Agnarr, RZ
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td class="grid_col2" align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									TWO to GO! - 
									8/7/2005 8:11:20 PM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									Well ORians.......the time is near we have bested Carpin and Bert to the end. Now we have added Agnarr to our Kill List, he too shall be defeated by the strength of OR. Our Kill List now contains the following.....Saryrn, LMM, Agnarr, and Tallon/Vallon Zek. Congrats to all those whom stand by your fellow ORians and show support both on official and nonofficial raids. Your Leads are proud of you all....now we just need to stay focused on these last few PoP Gods and we will reach Elementals together. On a side note once Saryrn cycle is done we will be adding our last PoP God.........Rallos Zek the Warlord.
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td>
								<div class="newsSeperator">&nbsp;</div>
							</td>
	</tr><tr>
		<td align="Center">
								<p class="newsTitle">
									Saryrn and her little bird, too! - 
									6/8/2005 6:35:34 AM
								</p>
								<div class="newsBody">
									After many ORians spent long hours helping to get Jetta's Saryrn key, we tackled Saryrn for the first time last night!&nbsp; It was a long raid, but thank goodness not as long as reports indicated.&nbsp; We went through all the mini bosses and took out Keeper of Sorrows on our way up.&nbsp; After struggling through the "getting there" part (which we couldn't have done without help from Darknyss and Irinar), Saryrn was a breeze.&nbsp; Besides getting the flags, we took home six different upgrades so the raid was a great success!<br /><br />Great job by everyone: leads and our raiders!<br /><br />New to OR?&nbsp; Please visit <a href="/forums/threadlist.aspx?fid=7194">this link</a> and read the posts marked "READ ME."<br />
								</div>
							</td>
	</tr>
